# Categories of AI Use

Now that you've explored when and how to use AI responsibly, let's look at some common ways educators use AI in their work.

Many AI-supported tasks fall into three categories: planning and preparation, communication and materials creation, and reflection and improvement.

<div style="display:grid; gap:16px; max-width:90%; margin:0 auto; font-family:ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial; color:#292F36;">

<!-- Card 1 -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:160px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/26c7cee156eb4de81ef0f03d54404d5e-Screenshot 2026-04-09 at 11.39.48 AM.png" 
     alt="Planning illustration" 
     style="width:100px; height:100px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Planning and Preparation</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
AI can support instructional design before teaching begins.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">This might include:</div>
<ul style="margin:0 0 12px 20px; padding:0; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
<li>Brainstorming lesson ideas or activities</li>
<li>Designing assessments and learning experiences</li>
<li>Aligning instruction to standards and goals</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

<!-- Card 2 -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:160px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/bbc956fe61b854eca56e743d69da30e9-Screenshot 2026-04-09 at 11.39.44 AM.png" 
     alt="Planning illustration" 
     style="width:100px; height:100px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Communication and Materials Creation</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
AI can help create and refine materials used with students and families.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">This might include:</div>
<ul style="margin:0 0 12px 20px; padding:0; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
<li>Creating handouts, slides, and classroom resources</li>
<li>Writing parent emails and updates</li>
<li>Revising language for clarity, tone, or readability</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

<!-- Card 3 -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:160px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/f350733c22d0ac7a2a97019e2e957dbe-Screenshot 2026-04-09 at 11.39.52 AM.png" 
     alt="Planning illustration" 
     style="width:100px; height:100px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Reflection and Improvement</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
AI can support reflection and continuous improvement.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">This might include:</div>
<ul style="margin:0 0 12px 20px; padding:0; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
<li>Reviewing lesson plans or assessments</li>
<li>Identifying gaps in alignment or rigor</li>
<li>Exploring ways to support different learners</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

</div>
MARKDOWN
